    "done_when": "Read section 23 of crew-runtime-positive-controls first. The read-only audit found its first half already met: the reservation is deliberately host-global, and the guard documents its reach (reservation_path in reckon/crew/placement.py, _refuse_over_reservation_roster in reckon/crew/dispatch.py). What remains is the reach stated where a project arms a placement. The reservation's hold path in reckon/crew/placement.py (_ensure_reservation_locked) and its adoption path return a detail that today names only the cap. They now state that the roster cap counts every project's placed live runs on this host, not only the holding project's, and they name the projects with placed live runs counted against it at that moment. The published record carries the same reach as a field, so a reader of the reservation file sees it too. tests/test_reservation_states_its_reach.py holds a reservation in a temporary config home, with the scheduler stubbed and live pointers from two projects present. It asserts that the detail and the record name the host-wide reach and both projects, and it fails at your base. Existing tests reaching the reservation hold, adoption and roster guard keep passing; grep tests/ for publish_reservation, _ensure_reservation_locked, RESERVATION_ROSTER_LIMIT and reservation to build the gate. Record the outcome in docs/evidence/fragments/crew-runtime-positive-controls/reservation-states-its-reach.html. Run `date -u` first and treat that instant as your start; your deadline is 60 minutes later. Write your manifest before starting any long command. Run both gate arms with pytest-xdist (-n 8 --timeout=300), never serially. Run the base arm, from a `git archive` extraction of your base under /tmp in a directory named for this run, and then the head arm, each in the foreground: a background command dies when your turn ends. Keep the gate to the test files that reach your change, tens of files rather than hundreds. Each arm uses its own basetemp outside any repository and writes to its own new log path, which it never overwrites. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder. Each log names its revision on the first line as revision= followed by the full sha, and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
